  "notes": "Baroque-and-percussion chamber-pop producer/arranger. The documented signature is a percussion one and it is the model's spine: \"drum programming plus layered live percussion is his documented signature — tambourine, shaker and hand drums stacked over a programmed kick/snare; the kit is rarely a plain rock kit.\" So `percs.densityPerBar` runs 5—9, the highest in this section, across four hand-percussion lanes at a forward gain, while the kick and snare stay programmed and tight — the split between a gridded kit and hand-played percussion is authored as an uneven `timingJitterMs`, low on kick and snare and high on the perc lanes. `hihat.base` is 8th at a low fill density with no roll vocabulary, because the entry says the percussion stack replaces the hats. Harmony is his training: \"classical-harmony-trained (studied classical harmony at Columbia), so expect functional voice-leading, inverted-bass motion, suspensions and harpsichord/organ-idiomatic voicings inside pop forms\", which is `topVoiceStepwise` true, `susSubstitutionProb` 0.44, a ii—V—I family and `close` voicing. No `bass808` block: \"no 808 idiom. Synth-programmed or played bass with a walking, contrapuntal line under the vocal\", so the bassline is `independent_riff` at 0.28 with a full walking passing-tone set. \"Loops are 4 or 8 bars with real motion, and countermelody is a keyboard or string line rather than a synth pad\" is the `answer_lick` counter and the absence of `vamp`; \"arrangements are dense but each layer is thin and distinct\" is the quiet velocity tier table under a high perc count. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a high-medium rating because the drum and harmonic numbers are INFERRED: the research documents an instrument list and a training, not a pattern. `bpm.mode` 115 is the midpoint of the stated 90—140 band.",
